				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/golden-shadow-inc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6922639); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6922639&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607758630" alt="Golden Shadow Inc" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6922639)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/golden-shadow-inc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6922639); return false;" >Golden Shadow Inc</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607757623 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Dec 2020 07:20</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13912704/deus-comedenti-translation:god-eater">Deus Comedenti (Translation: God Eater)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842793">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, Kafkaesque themes</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> It will be presented as an SCP Entry. The main narrative will be played out through the discovery logs and attached notes.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> There is a machine called &quot;Deus Comedenti&quot;, latin for &quot;God Eater&quot;. It was built to kill and harvest the energy of a God, but this fact is implied rather than told outright.<br />
The machine can also be used to harvest energy from any sentient life(on par with humans, but not animals).<br />
It comes attached with a tower-like battery the size of a 2 story building. Even though each individual human provides a lot of power (in terms of electricity), it takes the equivalent of a genocide of tragic proportions to fill it even an 1/8th of the way. It was 1/3 full as found. The storage can contain a humongous amount of power because of it's intended purpose.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
Basically this is set sometime in the near future. Oil is almost obselete, and cars and the like which used to run on oil have been adapted to use electricity.</p>
<p>In this setting, the Foundation finds that India has been utilising the machine to meet the vast energy demands of the country. India's current biggest import is oil, so if oil is replaced it makes sense that the country would try to find an alternative way to produce energy, so as to reduce necessary imports. In fact large solar power plants are already being built in real life.</p>
<p>The energy obtained from the machine is 'laundered' through the solar power plants.</p>
<p>The scheme was introduced as a stop gap till a better energy source could be developed, but then inertia took hold. Since not many people were aware of it at any given time, and it served the purpose well, successive govts. decided it was easier to keep using it than to develop entirely new costly energy sources.</p>
<p>The human input is secretly obtained from prisons, and occasionally political prisoners are used.</p>
<p>India in this setting becomes a major proponent of clean energy, since it has a way to produce a lot of it, and becomes a leading energy exporter, creating another incentive for the govt not to discontinue the program.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
- Government approved systemic killing responsible for bringing basic amenity to society, with the general public being unaware of where the &quot;clean energy&quot; comes from<br />
-Creation of energy via human sacrifice, facilitated by a machine created to kill a divine entity and harvest power from it, following E=MC^2.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Let me know if the idea seems a bit too political or targeted. That's my main concern.</p>

