														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842786">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A coin that flips itself every 3 seconds, landing on the skull side kills someone, landing on the wailing face has no effect. Article more relies on what is done to contain the SCP rather than the relatively simple idea itself</p>
<p>Central Narrative: This coin has by all means tested thus far been able to flip itself despite any non-anomalous or anomalous means. Because of it's nature, killing any human that is closest to it, the foundation attempts to hide it in an area with high death rates. At the time an ICU unit in a nearby hospital is surmised to be the best temporary candidate (this is before they understand how the SCP carries out the killing), until after the deaths of many staff and visitors to the ICU, they deduce that the coin is only based on proximity. The foundation also figures out the coin may work on humanoid anomalies, although they are hesitant to test it as the transport of the coin is rarely successful, and will only be moved from one site to another based on sheer luck. To avoid any sort of person or group discovering the incident, they place the SCP within a satellite orbiting earth, so that any death it may cause is seemingly extremely random, and has no way of being traced.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: Instant death is in the hands of a coin toss, but it cannot be contained</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I do worry that this concept isn't all that interesting, in that the SCP itself is a tad mundane. Any ideas to add to the narrative or aspects of the SCP would be greatly appreciated as I'm struggling to make this something that I find super interesting.</p>

