			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842778">
									

<p>You've got three basic problems here:</p>
<p>1) You're over-thinking the containment procedures. There's no reason why it shouldn't be put into a vault of its own and the combination basically lost. It just sounds like you have a lot of security measures that are doing nothing but wasting guard time checking them out. Putting it in a vault would take care of that problem.</p>
<p>2) If you want to make this into a time bomb of some sort then keep in mind that you could find paperwork on the safe. People always forget that these things have a history. There's also the question of what happens when the -1s/-2s hit some sort of critical mass.</p>
<p>3) The problem is that you have a simple SPC and you're trying to make this too complicated while working it out as you go. Figure out where you want to go with it first and then charge into it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
